{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114198","id":3117755347,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc651SvT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114198","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114198.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114198.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114198","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114198/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114198/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114198/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1c16c4fdcca63fca5112925aac8d09de0fe3dba1","number":114198,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add ability for Area3D to detect/influence SoftBody3D with Jolt Physics","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #111993.\r\n\r\nThis adds support for interactions between `Area3D` and `SoftBody3D` when using Jolt Physics as the 3D physics engine.\r\n\r\nThis PR also makes it so that the area's overlap signals are emitted whenever a soft body enters/exit its shapes, which is not something Godot Physics supports. As such, this is considered a breaking change, as the signal will now be emitted at times when they previously weren't, and for node types that previously were never passed to it.\r\n\r\nTo work around this breaking change you simply need to configure your collision layers/masks in such a way that the interactions between the relevant `Area3D` and `SoftBody3D` are ignored.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":955079684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw5NTUwNzk2ODQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/breaks%20compat","name":"breaks compat","description":"","color":"b64245","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","number":24,"state":"closed","title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co